  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">We Effect EU-Uganda 2020-2023</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">We Effect EU-Uganda 2020-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsens &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;l &#xe4;r att &quot;contribute to improved livelihoods of young women and men in Arua and Adjumani districts through creation of green employment options and strengthening youth governance, advocacy and decision-making capacities at local and national levels&quot;.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">We Effect har ans&#xf6;kt om finansiering av egeninsats om 951 552 SEK f&#xf6;r EU-projektet &quot;Green Livelihoods Youth (GLY) Project&quot; f&#xf6;r perioden 2020-2023.

Insatsen syftar till att: 

1. &quot;Contribute to improved livelihoods of young women and men in Arua and Adjumani districts through creation of green employment options and strengthening younth governance, advocacy and decision-making capacities at local and national levels&quot;. 

We Effect kommer att arbeta i samverkan med tv&#xe5; civilsamh&#xe4;llesorganisationer: Insamlingsstiftelsen Vi Planterar Tr&#xe4;d, och Uganda National Farmers Federation (UNFFE). We Effect har det &#xf6;vergripande ansvaret f&#xf6;r projektets implementering och koordinering. 

Den aktuella insatsen har EU-kommissionens referensnummer EuropeAid/165220/DD/ACT/UG-1. Insatsen har en total budget p&#xe5; 450 000 EUR, vilket motsvarar cirka 4 844 423 SEK. Av detta har We Effect beviljats 360 000 EUR fr&#xe5;n EU-kommissionen och ans&#xf6;ker om 951 552 SEK (cirka 20 %) fr&#xe5;n Sida.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">We Effect has applied to Sida for funding of 951 552 SEK to carry out the EU-Project &quot;Green Livelihoods Youth (GLY) Project&quot; during the period 2020-2023. 

The project aims to: 

1. Contribute to improved livelihoods of young women and men in Arua and Adjumani districts through creation of green employment options and strengthening youth governance, advocacy and decision-making capacities at local and national levels. 

We Effect will collaborate with two civil society organisations: Vi Agroforestry, and the co-applicant, Uganda National Farmers Federation (UNFFE). We Effect has the overall responsibility for the coordination and implementation of the project. 

The contribution has the EU Commission reference number EuropeAid/165220/DD/ACT/UG-1. The contribution&apos;s budget is 450 000 EUR, which corresponds to approximately 4 844 423 SEK. The requested support from Sida is 951 552 SEK which corresponds to approximately 20% of the total budget.</narrative>
  </description>
